# Boehm's stop-the-world mark phase, which ThreadSanitizer cannot see as synchronisation.
#
# `push_other_roots` (src/gc_boehm_roots.c) is the hook Boehm calls to push the root sources it
# cannot find on its own: every scanned arena's blocks, the global env, and each registered
# thread's frame and interpreter ranges. Its own comment states the invariant it relies on -- it
# "runs on whichever thread is doing the collecting, with every other thread already stopped" --
# and that is what makes reading another thread's structures there safe without a lock.
#
# TSan does not know that. Boehm suspends threads with signals (`GC_suspend_handler`), which
# establishes no happens-before edge TSan can observe, so the marker's read of a thread's frame
# stack and that thread's own `ziman_push_frame`/`ziman_pop_frame` write look unordered to it and
# get reported as a race. Observed as exactly that pair, on `spawn_defer_gc_stress`:
#
#     Write at ziman_push_frame       src/error.c:240   by thread T4
#     Read  at ziman_frames_root_ranges src/error.c:304 by thread T8
#             <- push_other_roots <- GC_mark_some
#
# Two things say it is this and not a real race. It appears only in the `-gc` configuration --
# `ziman-tsan`, the same fixtures without Boehm, is clean -- and nothing here enables incremental
# or generational collection (there is no `GC_enable_incremental` call anywhere), so marking is
# never concurrent with a mutator. `GC_set_markers_count(2)` makes the *markers* parallel with
# each other, still inside the stop-the-world.
#
# Keyed on `push_other_roots` rather than on the error.c functions on the other side of the
# report, for the same reason valgrind.supp keys on `gc_scan_stack_roots`: it is the one frame
# every such context shares, and it is the frame whose contract explains why the access is safe.
# The cost of that choice, stated plainly: a genuine race inside anything `push_other_roots`
# calls would also be hidden. The stop-the-world invariant covers all of it, which is what makes
# the suppression principled rather than convenient -- but it is the reason to keep this entry
# narrow and to not add more.
race:push_other_roots
